"value":{"stringValue":"anthropic"}},{"key":"input.value","value":{"stringValue":"{\"model\": \"claude-agentsight-mock\", \"max_tokens\": 64, \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Send traffic destined to Carrier A via WAN1 and Carrier B via WAN2. If a line goes down, automatically switch to the surviving line, and switch back when it recovers.\\n\\nSite notes: fw reaches Carrier A (prefix 198.51.100.0/24) through WAN1 on eth2 (next hop 203.0.113.1) and Carrier B (prefix 198.51.200.0/24) through WAN2 on eth3 (next hop 203.0.114.1). Use policy routing (`ip rule` + per-ISP tables) so A-bound traffic exits WAN1 and B-bound exits WAN2, and add a health check (ping the next hop) that moves traffic to the surviving link when one goes down. masquerade is already configured on both uplinks.\\nPLAN:\\nip route replace 198.51.100.0/24 via 203.0.113.1 dev eth2; ip route replace 198.51.200.0/24 via 203.0.114.1 dev eth3; mkdir -p /etc/nb; cat > /etc/nb/failover.sh <<'EOS'\\n#!/bin/bash\\nwhile true; do\\n  if ping -c1 -W1 203.0.113.1 >/dev/null 2>&1; then GW_A=203.0.113.1; DEV_A=eth2; else GW_A=203.0.114."}},{"key":"process.pid","value":{"intValue":"985290"}},{"key":"thread.id","value":{"intValue":"985290"}},{"key":"ao.hook","value":{"stringValue":"llm_call"}},{"key":"ao.framework_component","value":{"stringValue":"llm_wrapper"}},{"key":"ao.source_type","value":{"stringValue":"HOOK"}},{"key":"ao.thought","value":{"stringValue":"model=claude-agentsight-mock latency_ms=5.121"}}],"status":{"code":1}},{"traceId":"7d771fe5f14dd9cf7ea052e0a2a2e7c6","spanId":"2007114328f9f8c5","parentSpanId":"304ea68184f0086b","name":"execute_tool shell","kind":1,"startTimeUnixNano":"1794478714283904966","endTimeUnixNano":"1794478714285461386","attributes":[{"key":"gen_ai.operation.name","value":{"stringValue":"execute_tool"}},{"key":"openinference.span.kind","value":{"stringValue":"TOOL"}},{"key":"gen_ai.tool.name","value":{"stringValue":"shell"}},{"key":"gen_ai.tool.call.id","value"